  "note": "First election for the restored council, which had been dissolved on 6 March 1934 and run by a commissioner (Belfast News-Letter, 7 March 1934). The boundary had been extended and the city divided into five wards of four seats. Results were declared early on 19 September; about 55 per cent of the electorate voted. \"The Unionists also made a clean sweep in the North-East Ward\"; no label is printed against W. R. Johnston. The report gives the ward's \"total poll\" as 1,278."
